"""
Explores a multi-step funnel (quiz / VSL / lead-capture SPA) the way visitors
do, and captures every screen it can reach as its own page.

Funnel builders (inlead, Typebot-likes, Perspective, hand-rolled React) keep
the whole funnel inside ONE URL: clicking an answer swaps the DOM for the next
screen. A single snapshot of the first screen is a clone of 1/N of the funnel.

The result is a GRAPH, not a line: different answers can lead to different
screens (the "just researching" answer that leaves for another ending).

  1. PRIMARY PASS: from the first screen keep taking the first answer / the
     most call-to-action looking button until the funnel leaves the site, hits
     a dead end, or comes back to a screen already known. Every screen is
     observed for a while first (what appears LATER, and when), then
     snapshotted without touching the live app (capture_engine.snapshot works
     on a detached clone).
  2. BRANCH PASS: for every screen with several answers, the other answers
     are tried too. The app cannot be rewound, so each try replays the path
     from the start on its own page (several at once). A new screen found this
     way is explored like the primary pass; a known one just becomes an edge.
  3. WIRING: every answer / button is pointed at the screen it really leads to.

Nothing the walker does may reach the original owner's systems: non-GET
fetch/XHR (lead registration, webhooks) are answered locally, analytics are
swallowed, window.open / navigations to another site are intercepted and
recorded as the funnel's exit (never followed).
"""
